  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Boons and bonuses" id="9f9f-8789-1a22-d3d4" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="0" type="upgrade">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Boons" id="edee-8142-726d-35cd" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="9588-4200-697f-615f"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Forlorn Hope" id="f9c4-2402-9c3d-72f7" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8e4f-1814-7c75-b130" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Forlorn Hope" id="2812-af87-d0dd-6722" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">A single unit in the General’s Force that has been deployed at the start of the Clash gains the Vanguard (X”) special rule, with an (X) value 2” higher than its Speed. (For example, a unit with Speed 6” would gain the Vanguard (8”) special rule.)
If the chosen unit already has the Vanguard (X ) special rule it uses the highest (X) value of the two available.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Ready For Anything" id="e393-43dc-b40b-ba03" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="9e6a-b059-0317-f0d7" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="20"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Ready For Anything" id="9338-7dd2-1309-4251" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">A single unit in the General’s Force that has been deployed at the start of the Clash begins the Clash with the On Lookout status.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Countercharge" id="c6ca-6cdd-36ec-9e98" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d234-abb2-8945-39fd" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="30"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Countercharge" id="ed31-3522-8df1-639a" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">Once per Round, the General can issue this Special Command to one of their units that has the On Lookout status, in place of declaring Opportunity Fire.


If the Command is successfully issued, the unit immediately makes a Charge manoeuvre, ending in contact with the active enemy unit.


This unit then immediately makes a Close Quarters Attack. (The active enemy unit can Retaliate as normal, if it has a Melee attack.) After doing so, this unit loses its On Lookout status.




Note: This effectively counts as declaring Opportunity Fire, meaning that a General cannot use this Special Command and Opportunity Fire in the same turn.
 
If the unit is unable to end its Charge manoeuvre in contact with the active enemy unit, this Special Command cannot be issued.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Headstrong Commander" id="f721-cf09-644b-68ee" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4c96-2c45-3f8f-f607" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="45"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Headstrong Commander" id="cbfa-f477-dad4-494b" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">During the Draw Cards step of each Ready Phase, after drawing cards from their Command &amp; Conquest deck, the General can choose to draw one additional card and add it to their Hand.
If they do, they must then discard one card from their Hand.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Tempered Sturginium Blades" id="6570-df16-38fb-4ee3" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="308e-041c-37e8-ac1d" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="40"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Tempered Sturginium Blades" id="380f-e09b-94de-2fd3" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">Once per Round, when an Infantry or Cavalry unit in this Force makes a Close Quarters Attack, its General can discard a card from their hand before making the Attack Roll.


If they do so, this  Close Quarters Attack is made with the Devastating weapon quality.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Enhanced Alchemy" id="9eb6-6111-e892-b95e" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="8" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="aa26-5727-b6ba-9df0" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="50"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Enhanced Alchemy" id="b0a5-49b3-782f-4867" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">Once per Clash, at the start of a Round, the General can declare that they will use this Boon. Until the end of the Round, the effective range (X”) of any Obfuscating and Corrosive Fumes special rules belonging to their units is increased by 2”.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Battlegroup Bonus:" id="02ca-347c-d9ee-2c40" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4051-34ed-5833-473e" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="8baf-a893-0215-a8a2" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="name" type="append" value="The Celestian Guards">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="bbc0-6a5e-83e1-c5c1" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="name" type="append" value="The Swooping Crane">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="ffdd-f693-a84d-a1ca" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="name" type="append" value="For The Empire!">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="02e1-b891-584c-0c8e" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="name" type="append" value="None">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="d650-b893-9963-2882" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="name" type="append" value="Ei, Ei! Oh!">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="018c-a86e-32e7-92a7" childName="Bushido Aux BattleGroup" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="The Celestian Guards (Command)" id="51e2-5046-9f96-6771" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">This Battlegroup’s General can issue this Special Command to an Empire unit immediately before making a Discipline Test for it.


If the Command is successfully issued, the unit gains a +2 Discipline Bonus for the test.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="bbc0-6a5e-83e1-c5c1" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
            <profile name="The Swooping Crane (Command)" id="a0e5-3bea-f416-c74d" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">This Battlegroup’s General can issue this Special Command to an Empire unit at the start of its Movement Step.


If the Command is successfully issued, the unit increases its Speed by 2” during this step.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="ffdd-f693-a84d-a1ca" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
            <profile name="For The Empire!" id="6f41-43ec-01f9-bb2d" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">When Checking Visibility for a Ranged Attack made by an Empire unit, this Battlegroup’s General can discard a
Command &amp; Conquest Card from their hand to ignore a single friendly Empire unit of Size 2 or less.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="02e1-b891-584c-0c8e" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
            <profile name="None" id="73a4-f45c-c027-073d" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">Unlike most Battlegroups, the Empire Super-Heavy Auxiliary Battlegroup does not have a Commander, or a Commander Bonus.


This is intentional!</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="d650-b893-9963-2882" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Ei, Ei! Oh! (Command)" id="53f5-1655-5db5-9e74" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">At the end of a *Samurai* unit’s Activation, this Battlegroup’s General can attempt to issue a Special Command to it.
If this Special Command is successfully issued, it cannot be issued again until the next Round.
If the Command is successfully issued, this General can select a single enemy unit that is within 6” of the activated
*Samurai* unit. If the *Samurai* unit can draw Clear or Obscured Line of Sight to this enemy unit, a friendly *Ashigaru*
unit that can confirm Target Acquisition to this enemy unit can make a Ranged Attack against it. This attack has
an additional Combat Rating Penalty.
This attack can be made even if this friendly *Ashigaru* unit has the Activated status. If this *Ashigaru* unit has the On
Lookout status, it does not lose that status for performing this attack.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="018c-a86e-32e7-92a7" childName="Bushido Aux BattleGroup" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Honour in Death" id="be78-647a-59d9-c514" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="55a8-2af8-2b50-55a5" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="e58e-982d-7630-5342" value="30"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Honour in Death" id="6caa-a81e-c24c-9f3e" hidden="false" typeId="3f77-4198-5794-9684" typeName="Boons">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="b7f2-49d8-a49a-0b0f">When a *Samurai* unit is Annihilated, before removing the
last model in this unit from play, this Battlegroup’s
General can issue a Special Command. If the Command is
successfully issued, this unit can immediately make a
single Close Quarters Attack against one enemy Light or
Heavy unit within 5” of this unit. The enemy unit does not
make a retaliatory attack. If possible, this attack must be
made against the unit which Annihilated this unit.


After resolving this action, the last model of this unit is
immediately removed. A unit that is Annihilated while it is
Embarked cannot be issued this Special Command.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
